From 14119124685f25587ad06b194e118e8c8f23868e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:14:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] Bugfix: base the vertex label arrays gathered by
 distributed ordering writers [report R. Perry]

`dorderSave()` and `dorderSaveTree2()` gathered the vertex labels of
all processes into an un-based array, using the based process
displacement array, so that the root process wrote `baseval` cells
past the end of the array. `dorderSave()`, which based the array only
afterwards, then printed the label of the previous vertex on every
line, the first one being uninitialized; the tree and mapping writers,
which index the array with based vertex numbers, read past its end.

Base the label array before gathering, as `dmapSave()` does since
commit 4290e22, and add a based, labeled graph to the `dgord` checks.

Refs: DMO-02
